.TH std::indirect_unary_predicate 3 "2026.11.10" "http://cppreference.com" "C++ Standard Libary"
.SH NAME
std::indirect_unary_predicate \- std::indirect_unary_predicate

.SH Synopsis
Defined in header <iterator>
template< class F, class I >

concept indirect_unary_predicate =
std::indirectly_readable<I> &&                  \fI(since C++20)\fP
std::copy_constructible<F> &&
std::predicate<F&, /*indirect-value-t*/<I>> &&

std::predicate<F&, std::iter_reference_t<I>>;

The concept indirect_unary_predicate specifies requirements for algorithms that call unary
predicates as their arguments. The key difference between this concept and std::predicate
is that it is applied to the type that I references, rather than I itself.

